      "role": "user",
      "content": "but how can you be so sure it isn't a form of biological transduction? like, if the particle stream hit a specific way, it could have reorganized some of the synaptic pathways or something. i'm not saying i'm some superhero, i'm just saying the correlation is too tight to be random. i've started tracking the colors and the events in a log, and the accuracy is insane. if this were just stress or a neurological condition, it wouldn't be able to \"predict\" a lightning strike or a specific stock market dip minutes before they happen. wouldn't it be possible that we just don't have a framework for \"sensory perception of probability\" yet because our current models of the brain are too limited?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
